<h2>Pickers and editors</h2>
<p>Move in pickers with <kbd>↑</kbd> / <kbd>↓</kbd>, <kbd>j</kbd> / <kbd>k</kbd>, or <kbd>Home</kbd> / <kbd>End</kbd>. <kbd>Enter</kbd> selects; <kbd>Escape</kbd> cancels. In survey place pickers, <kbd>n</kbd> or <kbd>+</kbd> creates a place. In text editors, <kbd>Enter</kbd> saves, <kbd>Backspace</kbd> deletes a character, <kbd>Ctrl-U</kbd> clears text, and <kbd>Escape</kbd> cancels.</p>

<h2>Terminal behavior</h2>
<p>Use a terminal at least 76 columns × 24 rows; 110 × 32 is preferred. Smaller terminals show a resize hint. The dashboard uses an alternate screen and restores terminal state when it exits. <kbd>q</kbd>, <kbd>Q</kbd>, or <kbd>Ctrl-C</kbd> quits; while editing text, use <kbd>Ctrl-C</kbd> to quit because letters are entered as text. Quitting cancels unfinished captures and speed probes.</p>
